    "title": "Wounded woman walks a mile to S.F. hospital after shooting, police say - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Aldo Toledo ,\n23 hours ago A woman was shot on Tuesday and walked to a San Francisco hospital for treatment, police said. (Dan Hernandez/S.F. Chronicle) A woman was shot on Tuesday and walked to a San Francisco hospital, where she was treated for non-life-threatening injuries, police said.\nSan Francisco police responded at about 4:35 p.m. to the 2300 block of O’Farrell Street, near where Kaiser Medical Center is located, on reports of a person suffering from a gunshot wound.\nPolice found that the woman had been inside a vehicle on the 1100 block of Turk Street, near Jefferson Square Park, when she heard gunshots and realized she’d been struck. The hospital is about a mile from where she was shot.\nPolice did not disclose where the victim was hit.\nNo arrests have been made, authorities said. Anyone with information is asked to call the police department at 415-575-4444.\nSign up for San Francisco Chronicle newsletters here\nRead the original article on sfchronicle.com",
    "summary": "23 hours ago A woman was shot on Tuesday and walked to a San Francisco hospital for treatment, police said. Chronicle) A woman was shot on Tuesday and walked to a San Francisco hospital, where she was treated for non-life-threatening injuries, police said. San Francisco police responded at about 4:35 p.m. to the 2300 block of O’Farrell Street, near where Kaiser Medical Center is located, on reports of a person suffering from a gunshot wound.",
